    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlining the offensive output, despite both facing challenging right-handed starters. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a top-tier play with a score of 74.74; while Gerrit Cole\u2019s skill drags his efficiency down by 13%, the significant park factor boost and **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s elevated batting order position secure his spot. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a 16% park adjustment against Kyle Bradish, allowing his strong dynamic platoon profile to overcome the SP skill hurdle. **Sam Antonacci** is our surprise riser at a 67.67 score, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against G. Holmes and the premium value attached to his leadoff spot, which maximizes his opportunities to pad our stolen base category\u2014our most critical scarcity lever.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Wade Meckler** in the lineup at a 48.71 score, barely edging out **Nasim Nunez** on the bench. While **Nasim Nunez** provides high-end speed, his matchup against a high-skill arm like Jacob deGrom proved too daunting; the optimizer penalized **Nasim Nunez** heavily for the SP skill disparity and a bottom-of-the-order assignment. Conversely, **Wade Meckler** retains his utility status due to the projected leadoff role and a marginally more favorable matchup against Peter Lambert. We must proceed with caution regarding the pending lineups for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Coby Mayo**; should these projections shift significantly upon official posting, we will need to re-evaluate the utility of **Coby Mayo**, whose sub-50 score against Gerrit Cole leaves him as the most vulnerable piece of the starting puzzle.",
